[
  {
    "sha": "9b935c66a775f39bc85b5294cd4fbd6879e1e2d5",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDliOTM1YzY2YTc3NWYzOWJjODViNTI5NGNkNGZiZDY4NzllMWUyZDU",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-23T21:16:48Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-23T21:16:48Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(2d): one contour-parallel ring set for Pass starts at Auto, Inside and Outside\n\nAn area round a part (the 2D Offset Outside band) now has one ring set\nfor every start side: the offsets of the part, clipped to the\ncutter-centre area. Inside walks it from the part out, as before.\nOutside walks the same pieces mirrored (each piece reversed so climb\nstays climb, the outer edge first, the part wall last), so no ring\npiece ends on the part wall any more. Auto picks one of the two sides\nin one place (ring_side::resolve): Outside when the stock box leaves\nthe outer edge in air, else Inside. The resolved side drives the rings,\nthe links and the entry, so Auto is exactly the path of one side.\n\nPockets, the 3-D levels and the Adaptive plan keep their plans. The\nentry (#3746), the links (#3747) and the dead-end ramp (#3748) do not\nchange. Decision: docs/decisions/3744-one-ring-set.md.\n\nFixes #3744\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
