      "message": "fix(2d): share ring ends on the edge walk; no dead-end ramp round a part\n\nA ring end that the clip puts some microns off its boundary chord is now\nsnapped onto the boundary walk (within 0.1 um, the closing chord of a\nclosed walk included), so the verifier reads a touch, not a crossing.\nRound a part, Outside walks the Inside ring set and so enters as Inside\ndoes: the #3567 dead-end ramp marks stay only for pockets. On fig8, two\ndead-end ramps of the Auto (now Outside) pass crossed at shared depth.\n\nRefs #3744\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
