  {
    "sha": "6be6b1265d40e677647c829d17a16d41c17dec02",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDZiZTZiMTI2NWQ0MGU2Nzc2NDdjODI5ZDE3YTE2ZDQxYzE3ZGVjMDI",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-24T01:14:16Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-24T01:14:16Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(2d): fill rings where two rings of the one ring set merge\n\nRound a part, each band of the ring set is tested for stock that a\nflank of one ring meets and the swath of the other leaves (a merge of\nthe offsets of two sides of the part). There the band gets fills: the\nsame distance curve at half a step, and at a quarter and three quarters\nwhere the half leaves stock. A fill is a level curve of the distance\nfrom the part, so it crosses no ring, and Inside and Outside walk the\nsame fills (ring j is level 4 j; the mirror maps l to top + 4 - l).\n\nfig8 Outside: 495 -> 21 full-width meter points (single samples at 7\nring corners on 3 levels, named by the narrow note). No crossing from\neither side.\n\nRefs #3744\nRefs #3788\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
